{
  "id": "wholepage-public-wordlist",
  "status": "published",
  "title": "Public wordlist keys on complete LP2 pages",
  "question": "Do the 43 fixed public rune keys, at any phase in either GP29 Vigenère direction, produce an English-like complete unsolved page?",
  "reader_question": "Do the public dictionary keys decode a complete LP2 page?",
  "summary": "Across 33,990 complete-page outputs, none reached the predeclared English-score threshold. The best score was exceeded by 105 of 199 full-search shuffle controls.",
  "finding": "Zero of 33,990 whole-page outputs reached the -5.5 solved-reading threshold. The best (-6.5023) was equaled or exceeded by 105 of 199 full-search shuffled controls; nine solved-text and nine planted-key controls passed.",
  "limitations": "This checks only the 43 pinned keys, page-local repeating GP29 arithmetic at all phases and both signs, canonical transliteration, and this English score. A shuffled-runic null is a control for the search maximum, not a cipher model.",
  "next_steps": "If proposing a key, specify the exact source text or rune sequence, alignment, reset rule and success criterion; compare the resulting complete page against solved readings and a full-search control.",
  "outcome": "not-supported",
